  "domain": "robotics",
  "definition": "A collaborative robot (cobot) is an industrial robot designed and certified to work in direct physical proximity with human operators within a shared workspace, without requiring conventional hard safety guarding. Defined under ISO/TS 15066, cobots implement one or more of four collaborative operation modes \u2014 safety-rated monitored stop, hand guiding, speed-and-separation monitoring, and power-and-force limiting \u2014 each constraining robot behaviour so that human contact does not result in injury. Cobots typically feature lightweight, rounded structures, intrinsic force/torque sensing, and redundant safety-rated control architectures compliant with ISO 10218-1/-2.",
